From: Spack Project <spack@example.com>
Date: Sat, 9 Aug 2026 14:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Fix duplicate symbol error when building with ROCm

When building torchvision with ROCm support, the hipify process converts
torchvision/csrc/vision.cpp to vision_hip.cpp, but the build system then
compiles and links BOTH vision.cpp and vision_hip.cpp together. This causes
a linker error due to duplicate definition of vision::cuda_version().

The root cause is that hipify_python.hipify() is processing vision.cpp even
though the includes pattern is "torchvision/csrc/ops/cuda/*" which should not
match files in torchvision/csrc/ directory.

This patch explicitly excludes vision.cpp from hipification using the ignores
parameter, ensuring only the files under ops/cuda/ are converted to HIP.

Upstream issue: https://github.com/pytorch/vision/issues/TBD
Fixes build failure in CI job: https://gitlab.spack.io/spack/spack-packages/-/jobs/23839237

--- setup.py.orig	2026-08-09 13:59:24.211961011 -0700
+++ setup.py	2026-08-09 14:01:13.976910706 -0700
@@ -165,6 +165,7 @@
             project_directory=str(ROOT_DIR),
             output_directory=str(ROOT_DIR),
             includes="torchvision/csrc/ops/cuda/*",
+            ignores=("torchvision/csrc/vision.cpp",),
             show_detailed=True,
             is_pytorch_extension=True,
         )
